  <h2 id="market-reality">How thin is the market recognition, honestly</h2>

  <p>
    This section exists because most articles on niche combinations oversell them, and that does not help anyone make a real decision.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--gold">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">The honest read</p>
    <p>
      Commerce with computer science is a genuinely smaller, less conventional combination than most career paths this site covers. Search volume for the phrase is low. Job postings almost never use it as a label. There is no professional body, entrance exam, or standard curriculum built specifically around it the way there is for CA, BTech CSE, or even BCA.
    </p>
    <p>
      That does not mean it is worthless — the underlying skill combination (commerce domain knowledge plus data or coding ability) is genuinely in demand inside specific roles. But the demand is for the skills, not for the combination as a named identity. If you go into this expecting recruiters to recognise "commerce with CS" as a category, you will be disappointed. If you go in planning to build and present specific, provable skills for specific roles, the underlying opportunity is real, just narrower and less structured than a conventional degree path.
    </p>
  </div>

